        "original_id": "7cd1b2db-142d-5d64-8f05-9d5c2d036df5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Phelps, Klete Keller, Ryan Lochte, Peter Vanderkaay, Young Jeezy, Akon, Detail, Ray J, Lil Wayne, Beyoncé, Wiz Khalifa\n- Events: Athens games\n- Songs: \"I'm So Paid\", \"Sexy Can I\", \"How to Love\", \"Drunk in Love\", \"711\", \"We Dem Boyz\"\n- Roles: Olympians, swimmers, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Since the Athens games, the American relay team of Michael Phelps, Ryan Lochte, Peter Vanderkaay, and Klete Keller has been undefeated.\n- Michael Fred Phelps II was born on June 30, 1985.\n- Michael Phelps is an American former competitive swimmer.\n- Michael Phelps is the most decorated Olympian of all time, with 28 medals.\n- Young Jeezy's verse in the song \"I'm So Paid\" references fellow Olympian Michael Phelps.\n- Detail is a record producer best known for producing hit singles including Ray J's \"Sexy Can I,\" Akon's \"I'm So Paid,\" Lil Wayne's \"How to Love,\" Beyoncé's \"Drunk in Love\" and \"711,\" and Wiz Khalifa's \"We Dem Boyz.\"",
